  the clocks of a RG history to the reference readout: a one-step cone
  estimate gives a transfer datum <verbatim|TransferData> of the section
  against the holonomy.>|<cell|260>|<cell|\U>|<cell|tentative>>|<row|<cell|<hlink|G09|https://github.com/yang-mills-group/OpenAI-YM-20261028/blob/3456e5e75cf8d4cd558955a5c7638fba2d68f464/YM/Work/G09.lean>>|<cell|III>|<cell|Propagation
  of costs for a matched pair of trajectories (<verbatim|Duet>): coordinate
  difference is small relative to the remainder budget along the RG levels,
  by cones started at the coarsest index.>|<cell|235>|<cell|\U>|<cell|tentative>>>>>

  <subsection|Family H (Part III): fusion of forced
  activities><label|family-h-part-iii-fusion-of-forced-activities>

  <block|<tformat|<twith|table-width|1par>|<twith|table-hmode|exact>|<cwith|1|-1|1|-1|cell-hyphen|t>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-bborder|1ln>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-valign|bottom>|<table|<row|<cell|<strong|id>>|<cell|<strong|part>>|<cell|<strong|what
  it proves>>|<cell|<strong|lines>>|<cell|<strong|builds
  on>>|<cell|<strong|reading>>>|<row|<cell|<hlink|H01|https://github.com/yang-mills-group/OpenAI-YM-20261028/blob/3456e5e75cf8d4cd558955a5c7638fba2d68f464/YM/Work/H01.lean>>|<cell|III>|<cell|Fusion
  gas identity: the fused activities of the forced gathering equal the
  original gas times the exponential of the sum of the logarithms of the
  tap.>|<cell|268>|<cell|\U>|<cell|tentative>>|<row|<cell|<hlink|H02|https://github.com/yang-mills-group/OpenAI-YM-20261028/blob/3456e5e75cf8d4cd558955a5c7638fba2d68f464/YM/Work/H02.lean>>|<cell|III>|<cell|Budget
  for the forced startup merger: the fused activity obeys the K-bound with
  price v.>|<cell|81>|<cell|\U>|<cell|tentative>>|<row|<cell|<hlink|H03|https://github.com/yang-mills-group/OpenAI-YM-20261028/blob/3456e5e75cf8d4cd558955a5c7638fba2d68f464/YM/Work/H03.lean>>|<cell|III>|<cell|Forced-family
  and Moves receipts for fusion at fixed budget point P: the fused system is
  a forced family and has the face moves.>|<cell|336>|<cell|\U>|<cell|tentative>>|<row|<cell|<hlink|H04|https://github.com/yang-mills-group/OpenAI-YM-20261028/blob/3456e5e75cf8d4cd558955a5c7638fba2d68f464/YM/Work/H04.lean>>|<cell|III>|<cell|Fixed-period
  continuity of the forced gathering along a parameter curve
  (<verbatim|Curve>).>|<cell|162>|<cell|\U>|<cell|tentative>>>>>

  <subsection|Family I (Part III): marker supports and
  widths><label|family-i-part-iii-marker-supports-and-widths>

  <block|<tformat|<twith|table-width|1par>|<twith|table-hmode|exact>|<cwith|1|-1|1|-1|cell-hyphen|t>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-bborder|1ln>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-valign|bottom>|<table|<row|<cell|<strong|id>>|<cell|<strong|part>>|<cell|<strong|what
  it proves>>|<cell|<strong|lines>>|<cell|<strong|builds
  on>>|<cell|<strong|reading>>>|<row|<cell|<hlink|I01|https://github.com/yang-mills-group/OpenAI-YM-20261028/blob/3456e5e75cf8d4cd558955a5c7638fba2d68f464/YM/Work/I01.lean>>|<cell|III>|<cell|Support
  price for separated markers: B * card F \<less\>= 64 * coverNumber for a
  B^2-separated set of markers.>|<cell|84>|<cell|\U>|<cell|probable>>|<row|<cell|<hlink|I02|https://github.com/yang-mills-group/OpenAI-YM-20261028/blob/3456e5e75cf8d4cd558955a5c7638fba2d68f464/YM/Work/I02.lean>>|<cell|III>|<cell|(Assuming
  I01.) Resale from mixed and grain budgets: all tagged marker weights are
  priced, <verbatim|Radial> bound for the marker
  bands.>|<cell|182>|<cell|<hlink|I01|https://github.com/yang-mills-group/OpenAI-YM-20261028/blob/3456e5e75cf8d4cd558955a5c7638fba2d68f464/YM/Work/I01.lean>>|<cell|tentative>>|<row|<cell|<hlink|I03|https://github.com/yang-mills-group/OpenAI-YM-20261028/blob/3456e5e75cf8d4cd558955a5c7638fba2d68f464/YM/Work/I03.lean>>|<cell|III>|<cell|Geometry
  for the centred link tiling: alignment and pairwise spacing of the markers
  at stop level to cutoff.>|<cell|64>|<cell|\U>|<cell|tentative>>|<row|<cell|<hlink|I04|https://github.com/yang-mills-group/OpenAI-YM-20261028/blob/3456e5e75cf8d4cd558955a5c7638fba2d68f464/YM/Work/I04.lean>>|<cell|III>|<cell|Stop-width
  bookkeeping: positive widths and sublinear column product bound for the
  schedule of the given Family.>|<cell|130>|<cell|\U>|<cell|tentative>>>>>
</body>

